README.md-8-computer-architecture emulator: it runs real, unmodified operating systems on emulated
README.md-9-hardware, across several CPU families (MIPS, PowerPC, SuperH, ARM, Motorola 88K, …) and whole
README.md-10-machines (DECstation, Acer PICA/Jazz, SGI, macppc, Dreamcast, …) — CPU, MMU, interrupt
README.md-11-controllers, serial, framebuffers, SCSI/IDE disks, Ethernet NICs. It is educational/experimental
README.md-12-software, **not a trust or isolation boundary.**
