regress/README.md-205-**0 regressions**. Among the 13 is `macppc`, where upstream throws an AddressSanitizer
regress/README.md-206-heap-buffer-overflow that the current code no longer does — that is correction #23, found
regress/README.md-207-by this same technique years ago and now guarded by a standing check rather than a one-off.
regress/README.md-208-
regress/README.md:209:**A machine must be given a file or it never starts up.** `-E testmips` with no file prints
regress/README.md-210-a usage message and quits *before attaching any device* — a sweep written that way would
regress/README.md-211-test nothing and pass every time. Handing it a 500-byte dummy file makes it report
regress/README.md-212-`model:`, `cpu:`, `memory:` and attach hardware. Machines with sub-models additionally need
regress/README.md-213-`-e <subtype>`; without that, 13 of 37 never start.
