regress/README.md-248-### What this gate got wrong on its first run
regress/README.md-249-
regress/README.md-250-Both mistakes are the harness's recurring failure mode, so they are recorded rather than
regress/README.md-251-quietly fixed:
regress/README.md-252-
regress/README.md:253:1. It used `-e testmips`. That is the **subtype** flag; the machine flag is `-E`. Every
regress/README.md:254:   invocation produced `Sorry, emulation "" (subtype "testmips") is unknown.` — and the
regress/README.md-255-   gate compared that identical error across three builds and reported **22 checks
regress/README.md-256-   passing**. Upstream's own `configure` comment still shows `-e`; it predates the change.
regress/README.md-257-2. Its only guard was a 100-byte floor on output, which an error message clears easily.
regress/README.md-258-   **A floor proves volume, not validity.** Every case now asserts a format-specific
regress/README.md-259-   marker only the real loader can print — `ELF64 LSB`, `b.out`, `a.out` — so an error, a
