regress/README.md-274-
regress/README.md-275-Any gate that boots the same disk image more than once — or boots it under more than one
regress/README.md-276-build — has to use GXemul's `R:` prefix:
regress/README.md-277-
regress/README.md-278-```
regress/README.md:279:gxemul -e luna-88k -d R:liveimage-luna88k-raw-20250518.img boot
regress/README.md-280-```
regress/README.md-281-
regress/README.md-282-`R:` opens the base image **read-only** and routes every guest write into a temporary
regress/README.md-283-overlay that is discarded at exit. Plain `-d` opens it **read/write**, so the guest's
regress/README.md-284-writes land in the shared file and persist.
