.\_scratchpad\panel_20260831_054552\ollama_glm.txt:1:**VERDICT:** The brief's central observation rests on one unverified, load-bearing premise: that this fork's `fatal()` prints and *returns*. Nothing in the packet shows that. If it is false, the "HUH?" line held up as the announce-and-continue precedent is itself a kill — value-triggered, reachable by a plain byte write with stray bits, cheaper to trip than any width guard — and "13 live terminating calls" is not a count of kills, because the grep sees only line-initial `exit(1);`. One fact settles it: the body of `fatal()` in this fork. Second defect, packet-internal: Q3's premise ("read arms assign `odata`") is contradicted by the packet's own excerpt — neither inlined arm assigns `odata` at all. Assuming `fatal()` does return: the precedent settles *tone* (announce, don't exit) but not *disposition* — it is an unlatched masked-accept on a legal-width write, so copy its shape and not its latching. Provisional disposition: **decline + latched announce, `odata` set explicitly in the guard**. Five mutants survive "host survived and a message appeared"; listed under Q4.
.\_scratchpad\panel_20260831_054552\ollama_glm.txt:21:So: **copy the shape, not the latching.** Latch per house idiom, keep the per-register token, and do not let one latch bit serve all twelve arms (M3). Of the six options: delete is worst; silent decline discards diagnosability the house plainly wants; ACCEPT's premise is unsupported (P2); FAULT has no shown plumbing (settling fact: one existing device that raises a guest-visible fault from its access function); BACKED ACCEPT invents state no packet evidence says exists. Decline + latched announce is what the packet supports.
.\_scratchpad\panel_20260901_173956_500p3\ollama_deepseek.txt:11:**Q4.** The two new rows are not vacuous in the current state, but they are vacuous against a mask that includes only TB, because they do not exercise that bit. They also rely on `count(DRAW) == 0`; a targeted change to the decline message for those specific legal primitives could make them pass while still declining, but that would be a larger edit and likely caught by other rows if global. The primary vacuity is the missing TB dimension. (REASONED)
