.\_scratchpad\panel_514p2_20260908\grok.txt:1:I'll inspect the `#514` product, probe, and artifacts in `src/` first, then check the premises those six seats treated as given.Pass-1 panel notes and the actual palcode handler are next, so I can test the floor claim against the tree rather than the write-up.I'll read the pass-1 briefs, witness artifacts, and Alpha PAL docs next, then check whether the wrapper and census claims actually match the tree.Pass-1 seats and the architecture sources are next; I need to see which census and wrapper claims actually got corrected.I'll check the vacuity-floor rule, the `#507` probe, `alphatbinegsel` coupling, and whether `print` can accidentally yield `C`.**VERDICT: The one-identifier product is correct and sufficient. The witness is a real rung-3 red-then-green. The round is not complete as argued: clause (d) was misnamed, `a0 land` pins a value the architecture does not require, and the probe is blind to a hardcoded `v0 = 0x01000000`. None of that is an L2 floor breach. Do not owe a built `v0 = a0` mutant. Do not treat the `alphatbinegsel` re-baseline as a `#514` flush debt — this hunk did not touch the invalidate.**
.\_scratchpad\panel_514p2_20260908\grok.txt:79:- seed `SENT = CTX_C` (or any `S == C`). Broken PAL leaves v0 untouched; v0 is then C; `v0 ctx` goes green. This is the vacuity the seed exists to prevent, inverted.
.\_scratchpad\panel_514p2_20260908\ollama_glm.txt:19:**(d) by construction is acceptable here, and I'd push back on calling it an argument.** READ: the row is a constant equality, `v0_final` against `"0x%x" % CTX_C`; the three oracle constants are pairwise distinct and the probe *asserts* their distinctness; both sides use the same formatter, so no hex-width accident; and every other row is value-blind with all parse failures failing RED (`printed` returns `"absent"`, which fails every comparison). The only route to GREEN is the parsed value equaling C exactly. Of the three oracle cells, S is measured (2/4 pre-fix — the handler-never-writes-v0 world) and C is measured (4/4); the N cell needs nothing but `N ≠ C`. A built `v0 = a0` mutant would add only "the probe runs on a v0-writing build," and runnability is already evidenced twice. **A mutant is owed when the row's predicate could be satisfied by a wrong repair ("v0 changed"); this row's predicate cannot be.** The round owes one sentence recording that discharge, so pass 3 doesn't re-litigate. Caveat on scope: this discharges wrong-repair vacuity for the *return-value* contract only — see Q2.
.\_scratchpad\panel_514p2_20260908\ollama_minimax.txt:17:## Q1 — The vacuity floor, clause (d)
.\_scratchpad\panel_514p2_20260908\ollama_deepseek.txt:1:VERDICT: The one-line product fix is correct as stated, and the probe clears the vacuity floor for the shipped defect; however, the probe has a real coverage gap: it does not assert that the new context was actually installed. Q1(d) is acceptable analytically but is REASONED, not a measured mutant.
.\tools\README.md:25:| `pipeline/check_commit_attribution.py` | asks whether the LEDGER noticed the work that SHIPPED. On its first run, 33 of the 40 most recent commits were named by no row -- most legitimately, two sharply: a commit whose subject read "selfmutant6 CLOSED" against a row still marked held, and a row whose `commits` field named an unrelated device round. **Reports BOTH its own blindnesses on every run** -- row ids too short to match safely, and rows carrying commits that no subject ever names -- because a check that silently skips a third of its subjects while printing a green line is this project's newest named vacuity class. |
.\_scratchpad\panel_20260901_183841_pcc2p1\ollama_minimax.txt:1:**VERDICT: Reachability plausible but the device-dispatch link is not in the packet; Q1 disposition is decline + latched announce, but the ACCEPT premise cannot be fully checked without the read-path code; Q2 warrant is insufficient under the stated "measured delta or transferred warrant" rule because dev_pcc2 is single-instance per process; Q3 leave the two #119 sites; Q4 smallest mutant is `|=` → `=` in a per-arm bitmap, or — if a single shared bit is used — there is no `|=` to drop and the coarseness itself becomes the defect.**
.\_scratchpad\panel_20260901_183841_pcc2p1\ollama_minimax.txt:29:3. **Decline + latched announce.** Matches the in-file precedent from #119. Preserves a diagnostic. **Preferred.**
